__NAME__ - copy files to standard output

__NAME__ writes each file operand, or standard input, to standard output.


Requirements
------------
A Rust toolchain (cargo) and a POSIX make. No crates beyond std.


Installation
------------
__NAME__ is installed into the /usr/local namespace by default; override
PREFIX on the make command line.

Afterwards enter the following command to build and install __NAME__ (if
necessary as root):

    make clean install


Running
-------
    __NAME__ [-v] [file...]

See __NAME__(1).


Configuration
-------------
The configuration of __NAME__ is done by editing src/config.rs and
(re)compiling the source code. src/config.rs is copied from
src/config.def.rs on the first build; customisations are kept as patches
against src/config.def.rs.
